.he "ftruncate (2)                10/3/26                   ftruncate (2)"
.fo "				    -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
ftruncate
- truncate an open file to a length


.in -5
.bd
C
.in +5
.br
ftruncate(descriptor, length)
.br
long length;


.in -5
.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
.bd
Ftruncate
truncates the file named by descriptor to at most
length bytes.  The file must be open for writing and
must be a regular file.

If the file was longer, the data past length is lost
and the blocks that held it are returned to the free
list.  If the file was already at most length bytes,
nothing happens; a file is never made longer by this
call.


.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
A 0 indicates success, a -1 indicates failure.


.in -5
.bd
ASSEMBLER
.in +5
.br
